 "_label_space_note": "content sha256 fragments one document into several when it is captured at different scroll positions; the heading is the document's own identity claim. The heading space is the operative one and the hash space is reported as the pessimistic bound.",
 "verdict": "NOT SETTLED AT THIS n, AND THE HONEST ANSWER IS A LOOKUP TABLE FIRST. The best deterministic baseline -- (module, record type) -> document -- reaches 64.2% (95% Wilson CI 56.2%-71.5%) against 5.4% random, on n=148 pairs over 17 document labels. A learned retriever would have to exceed 71.5% before this evidence could tell it apart from the lookup table at all. Build the lookup table, instrument it, and let the residual decide whether a model is warranted.",
